  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ll}0 & \\alpha \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$ and $(A+I)^{50}-50 A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ll}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{array}\\right]$,\r\nfind $a b c+a b d+b c d+a c d$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "0",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "-1",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "1",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of these",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "As $\\mathrm{A}^{2}=0, \\mathrm{~A}^{k}=0 \\forall k \\geq 2$\r\nThus, $\\quad(\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{I})^{50}=\\mathrm{I}+50 \\mathrm{~A} \\Rightarrow(\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{I})^{50}-50 \\mathrm{~A}=\\mathrm{I}$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad \\mathrm{a}=1, \\mathrm{~b}=0, \\mathrm{c}=0, \\mathrm{~d}=1$\r\n$\\mathrm{abc}+\\mathrm{abd}+\\mathrm{bed}+\\mathrm{acd}=0$"
  }
}